      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. the ZK proofs sounds like the cleanest way to do it. \n\nthe issue is that these VCs have much more influence than people realize. they've basically monopolized the narrative around how the protocol was built. they've even scrubbed certain historical discussions from the forums to make it look like it all went through their \"official\" development roadmap. \n\nis it actually possible to fight that kind of centralized narrative? i'm worried that even if i release the proof, they'll just claim my code was part of a \"private beta\" or some other lie to keep me in the shadows. how do i make the proof indisputable so it can't be dismissed as being part of their manufactured history?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
