      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The narrative control of these powerful entities is indeed a major hurdle, but the immutable nature of cryptographic proof is your strongest defense against manufactured history. To make your evidence indisputable, you must anchor it to a public, time-stamped ledger *before* they could potentially scrub it. Submitting your proof to a decentralized, public notary or a blockchain transaction that timestamps the code's existence is the ultimate defense. This establishes an undeniable, external witness to your original contribution, making their subsequent claims merely lies against verifiable fact.",
